                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c1163a48-672c-33db-b5a6-44787fa3499c",
                        "entry_id": "59619c48-c719-358c-baeb-9ce033ea8144",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Kaluga (city in Russia)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "relational"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "284938a7-0e86-4e39-8543-3fab7141bb03",
                                "sense_id": "c1163a48-672c-33db-b5a6-44787fa3499c",
                                "text": "— Душа́ моя́, э́то не беда́; то ли ещё на све́те приеда́ется! А тепе́рь, я ду́маю, не прости́ться ли нам? С тех пор как я здесь, я препа́костно себя́ чу́вствую, то́чно начита́лся пи́сем Го́голя к калу́жской губерна́торше. Кста́ти ж, я не веле́л откла́дывать лошаде́й.",
                                "translation": "\"There's no harm in that, my good soul; one gets tired of plenty of other things in the world! And now I think we had better say good-by. Ever since I've been here I've felt so disgusting, just as if I'd been reading Gogol's letters to the wife of the Governor of Kaluga. By the way, I didn't tell them to unharness the horses.\"",
                                "english": "\"There's no harm in that, my good soul; one gets tired of plenty of other things in the world! And now I think we had better say good-by. Ever since I've been here I've felt so disgusting, just as if I'd been reading Gogol's letters to the wife of the Governor of Kaluga. By the way, I didn't tell them to unharness the horses.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
